Credits
-------

* linux-3ds (https://github.com/linux-3ds) — the Linux kernel port, the ARM11
  FIRM loader (firm_linux_loader) and the ARM9 SD/PXI firmware (arm9linuxfw)
  this project boots on, plus the base 3DS SD host controller driver.

* Android3DS / Octoblimp (https://github.com/Octoblimp/Android-Eclair-3DS) —
  an earlier Android 2.0 (Eclair) port to the same hardware.  Cyano3DS builds
  on it and reuses, adapted to this kernel and userspace:

    - the pre-mainline staging AR6K Wi-Fi driver and its Nintendo NWM firmware
      boot path (fetched from Octoblimp at a pinned commit by
      port/scripts/fix-wifi-octoblimp.py; Cyano3DS's changes to it are in
      port/kernel/patches/ath6k_legacy-cyano3ds.patch),
    - the AR6002 SDIO host-controller changes
      (port/kernel/drivers/platform/nintendo3ds/ctr_sdhc.c),
    - the resistive-touchscreen driver
      (port/kernel/drivers/platform/nintendo3ds/tsc/touch.c).

  Cyano3DS targets a later Android release (2.3.7 vs 2.0), but the Wi-Fi and
  touch bring-up started from that project's work.

* CyanogenMod and the Android Open Source Project — the userspace.

* The AR6014G Wi-Fi firmware is not shipped.  Each builder dumps it from their
  own console's NWM and carves it with port/scripts/nwm-extract.py; see the
  "Wi-Fi" section of docs/WIFI.md.

